---
interface Surface {
  name: string;
  commands: string;
}

interface Props {
  surfaces: Surface[];
}

const { surfaces } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="inventory-panel">
  <div class="inventory-heading">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">the generated command surface</span>
      <h3>Every branch, still namespaced.</h3>
    </div>
    <span class="inventory-count">10 APIs</span>
  </div>
  <div class="inventory-list">
    {surfaces.map((surface) => (
      <details class="inventory-item">
        <summary>
          <span>{surface.name}</span>
          <span class="inventory-summary-mark" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="inventory-commands"><code>{surface.commands}</code></div>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p>Run <code>grr &lt;service&gt; --help</code> and <code>grr schema</code> for the exact flags. The tree is generated from Google's Discovery Service - every method nests by resource (<code>grr gmail users messages list</code>, <code>grr drive files get</code>) with typed flags per parameter. <code>grr api list</code> and <code>grr api describe</code> are the flat, id-based equivalents.</p>
</div>
